cs2-name = Counter-Strike 2

cs2-integration = Counter-Strike 2 integration
cs2-integration-help = Uses Game State Integration, Valve's official system: CS2 itself sends each match's data to Archi Games on this PC (127.0.0.1, port 43117). Turning it on copies gamestate_integration_archigames.cfg into CS2's cfg folder; turning it off deletes it. It doesn't touch the game. Competitive, Premier, casual and Wingman matches played to the end on this PC, with Archi Games open, count.
cs2-integration-enable = Turn on
cs2-integration-disable = Turn off
cs2-integration-off = Off.
cs2-integration-waiting = On. Open CS2 (or restart it if it was already open): your account links itself as soon as the first data comes in.
cs2-integration-receiving = Receiving data from CS2.
cs2-integration-account = Steam account: { $name }
cs2-running = Counter-Strike 2 is open: each match is recorded when it ends.
cs2-closed = Counter-Strike 2 is closed.
cs2-last-match = Last recorded match: { $when }
cs2-error-not-found = CS2's folder wasn't found. Is it installed through Steam on this PC?
cs2-error-port = Another program is using port 43117; close it and turn the integration on again.
cs2-error-install = The file in CS2's cfg folder couldn't be written or deleted.
cs2-error-private = CS2 isn't sending this player's data.
cs2-error-network = No data is coming from CS2.

